note: schema.q:1:1 — N_NO_HORIZON: table conversations: `sync public` has no horizon, so every row of every group a device holds reaches it and stays; a device that holds many groups, or a public table that grows, pays for all of it at every cold start; measure what it costs with `check --residency`
  rewrite: sync public last 500 by .id
  guide: sync
  why: snapback4 why N_NO_HORIZON

note: schema.q:6:1 — N_NO_HORIZON: table members: `sync public` has no horizon, so every row of every group a device holds reaches it and stays; a device that holds many groups, or a public table that grows, pays for all of it at every cold start; `cap 100 by conversationId` bounds the rows per conversationId, not what a device acquires — `sync public` delivers every conversationId's rows to every device; measure what it costs with `check --residency`
  rewrite: sync public last 500 by .id
  guide: sync
  why: snapback4 why N_NO_HORIZON

